You are implementing bead vamsa-ywo.10: GEDCOM Import/Export UI for the vamsa family tree application.

## Context
- All backend is complete: parser, mapper, generator, server actions, API routes
- All tests passing: 471 total tests including 121 GEDCOM tests
- Target: Build user-facing components for import/export functionality
- Do NOT commit when done - just implement the code

## Task: Create Import/Export UI Components

### Part 1: GEDCOM Export Button Component

Create `src/components/admin/gedcom-export.tsx`:

A simple button component that:
- Shows "Export as GEDCOM" button
- On click, fetches from `/api/admin/gedcom/export`
- Downloads file as `family-tree-YYYY-MM-DD.ged`
- Shows loading state while fetching
- Shows success/error toast notifications
- Uses TanStack Query for the mutation

```typescript
'use client'

import { useState } from 'react'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { useToast } from '@/components/ui/use-toast'
import { Download, Loader2 } from 'lucide-react'

export function GedcomExportButton() {
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false)
  const { toast } = useToast()

  const handleExport = async () => {
    setIsLoading(true)
    try {
      const response = await fetch('/api/admin/gedcom/export')

      if (!response.ok) {
        const error = await response.text()
        throw new Error(error)
      }

      const blob = await response.blob()
      const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob)
      const a = document.createElement('a')
      a.href = url
      a.download = `family-tree-${new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0]}.ged`
      document.body.appendChild(a)
      a.click()
      URL.revokeObjectURL(url)
      document.body.removeChild(a)

      toast({
        title: 'Export successful',
        description: 'Your family tree has been exported as GEDCOM'
      })
    } catch (error) {
      toast({
        title: 'Export failed',
        description: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error',
        variant: 'destructive'
      })
    } finally {
      setIsLoading(false)
    }
  }

  return (
    <Button
      onClick={handleExport}
      disabled={isLoading}
      variant="outline"
    >
      {isLoading ? (
        <>
          <Loader2 className="mr-2 h-4 w-4 animate-spin" />
          Exporting...
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <Download className="mr-2 h-4 w-4" />
          Export as GEDCOM
        </>
      )}
    </Button>
  )
}
```

### Part 2: GEDCOM Import Component

Create `src/components/admin/gedcom-import.tsx`:

A full import workflow component with:
- File input (accept .ged files only)
- Validation preview before import
- Progress indication during import
- Results display (success/error)
- Uses server actions for import/validate

```typescript
'use client'

import { useState } from 'react'
import { validateGedcomFile, importGedcom } from '@/actions/gedcom'
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { useToast } from '@/components/ui/use-toast'
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
  DialogTrigger,
} from '@/components/ui/dialog'
import { Upload, AlertCircle, CheckCircle, Loader2 } from 'lucide-react'

type ImportState = 'idle' | 'validating' | 'preview' | 'importing' | 'success' | 'error'

export function GedcomImportDialog() {
  const [state, setState] = useState<ImportState>('idle')
  const [file, setFile] = useState<File | null>(null)
  const [preview, setPreview] = useState<any>(null)
  const [result, setResult] = useState<any>(null)
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false)
  const { toast } = useToast()

  const handleFileSelect = async (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
    const selectedFile = e.target.files?.[0]
    if (!selectedFile) return

    if (!selectedFile.name.endsWith('.ged')) {
      toast({
        title: 'Invalid file',
        description: 'Please select a .ged file',
        variant: 'destructive'
      })
      return
    }

    setFile(selectedFile)

    // Validate file
    setState('validating')
    try {
      const formData = new FormData()
      formData.append('file', selectedFile)
      const validation = await validateGedcomFile(formData)

      if (validation.valid) {
        setPreview(validation.preview)
        setState('preview')
      } else {
        setPreview(validation.preview)
        setState('error')
      }
    } catch (error) {
      toast({
        title: 'Validation failed',
        description: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error',
        variant: 'destructive'
      })
      setState('idle')
    }
  }

  const handleImport = async () => {
    if (!file) return

    setState('importing')
    try {
      const formData = new FormData()
      formData.append('file', file)
      const importResult = await importGedcom(formData)

      if (importResult.success) {
        setResult(importResult)
        setState('success')
        toast({
          title: 'Import successful',
          description: `Imported ${importResult.imported?.people} people and ${importResult.imported?.relationships} relationships`
        })
        // Reset after delay
        setTimeout(() => {
          setOpen(false)
          setState('idle')
          setFile(null)
          setPreview(null)
          setResult(null)
        }, 2000)
      } else {
        setResult(importResult)
        setState('error')
        toast({
          title: 'Import failed',
          description: importResult.message,
          variant: 'destructive'
        })
      }
    } catch (error) {
      toast({
        title: 'Import error',
        description: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error',
        variant: 'destructive'
      })
      setState('error')
    }
  }

  const resetForm = () => {
    setState('idle')
    setFile(null)
    setPreview(null)
    setResult(null)
  }

  return (
    <Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={setOpen}>
      <DialogTrigger asChild>
        <Button variant="outline">
          <Upload className="mr-2 h-4 w-4" />
          Import GEDCOM
        </Button>
      </DialogTrigger>
      <DialogContent>
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle>Import GEDCOM File</DialogTitle>
          <DialogDescription>
            Import a family tree from GEDCOM format
          </DialogDescription>
        </DialogHeader>

        {state === 'idle' && (
          <div className="space-y-4">
            <div className="flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-gray-300 p-6">
              <input
                type="file"
                accept=".ged"
                onChange={handleFileSelect}
                className="hidden"
                id="gedcom-file-input"
              />
              <label
                htmlFor="gedcom-file-input"
                className="cursor-pointer text-center"
              >
                <p className="text-sm font-medium">Click to select or drag and drop</p>
                <p className="text-xs text-gray-500">.ged files only</p>
              </label>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {state === 'validating' && (
          <div className="flex items-center justify-center p-6">
            <Loader2 className="h-6 w-6 animate-spin" />
            <span className="ml-2">Validating file...</span>
          </div>
        )}

        {state === 'preview' && preview && (
          <div className="space-y-4">
            <div className="rounded-lg bg-blue-50 p-4">
              <p className="text-sm font-medium text-blue-900">Preview</p>
              <p className="text-sm text-blue-700">
                {preview.peopleCount} people, {preview.familiesCount} families
              </p>
            </div>
            {preview.errors && preview.errors.length > 0 && (
              <div className="rounded-lg bg-yellow-50 p-4">
                <p className="text-sm font-medium text-yellow-900">Warnings</p>
                {preview.errors.map((error, i) => (
                  <p key={i} className="text-sm text-yellow-700">
                    {error.message}
                  </p>
                ))}
              </div>
            )}
            <div className="flex gap-2">
              <Button variant="outline" onClick={resetForm}>
                Cancel
              </Button>
              <Button onClick={handleImport}>
                Import
              </Button>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {state === 'importing' && (
          <div className="flex items-center justify-center p-6">
            <Loader2 className="h-6 w-6 animate-spin" />
            <span className="ml-2">Importing...</span>
          </div>
        )}

        {state === 'success' && result && (
          <div className="space-y-4">
            <div className="rounded-lg bg-green-50 p-4">
              <div className="flex items-center">
                <CheckCircle className="h-5 w-5 text-green-600" />
                <p className="ml-2 font-medium text-green-900">Import successful!</p>
              </div>
              <p className="mt-2 text-sm text-green-700">
                {result.message}
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {state === 'error' && (
          <div className="space-y-4">
            <div className="rounded-lg bg-red-50 p-4">
              <div className="flex items-center">
                <AlertCircle className="h-5 w-5 text-red-600" />
                <p className="ml-2 font-medium text-red-900">Error</p>
              </div>
              <p className="mt-2 text-sm text-red-700">
                {result?.message || 'Unknown error occurred'}
              </p>
              {result?.errors && result.errors.length > 0 && (
                <div className="mt-2 space-y-1">
                  {result.errors.map((error, i) => (
                    <p key={i} className="text-xs text-red-600">
                      {error.message}
                    </p>
                  ))}
                </div>
              )}
            </div>
            <Button onClick={resetForm} className="w-full">
              Try Again
            </Button>
          </div>
        )}
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  )
}
```

### Part 3: Admin Page Integration

Update `src/app/(dashboard)/admin/page.tsx` to include GEDCOM section:

```typescript
import { GedcomExportButton } from '@/components/admin/gedcom-export'
import { GedcomImportDialog } from '@/components/admin/gedcom-import'

export default function AdminPage() {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-8">
      {/* ... existing admin sections ... */}

      {/* GEDCOM Import/Export Section */}
      <section className="space-y-4">
        <div>
          <h2 className="text-lg font-semibold">GEDCOM Exchange</h2>
          <p className="text-sm text-gray-500">
            Import from or export to GEDCOM format for compatibility with other genealogy software
          </p>
        </div>
        <div className="flex gap-2">
          <GedcomImportDialog />
          <GedcomExportButton />
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Acceptance Criteria

1. ✓ Export button present on admin page
2. ✓ Export downloads .ged file with date in filename
3. ✓ Export shows loading state and success/error toast
4. ✓ Import dialog opens with file picker
5. ✓ Import validates .ged file only
6. ✓ Import shows validation preview before importing
7. ✓ Preview displays people and family count
8. ✓ Preview shows any warnings or errors
9. ✓ Import button proceeds after preview
10. ✓ Import shows loading state during process
11. ✓ Import shows success message with counts
12. ✓ Import shows error message on failure
13. ✓ Dialog closes automatically after success
14. ✓ User can retry on error
15. ✓ Components follow existing UI patterns (shadcn/ui)
16. ✓ Mobile responsive
17. ✓ Accessibility features (labels, descriptions)

When done, test the complete flow:
1. Export current family tree to GEDCOM
2. Import the exported file
3. Verify data matches
4. Test with sample GEDCOM files

Update bead status when complete: `bd update vamsa-ywo.10 --status=ready`

